# callable_bounds - a type parameter with a callable bound (`F: (T) -> U`) takes a capturing closure, a named function or a non-capturing lambda, in every callee shape: free functions in this module and another, methods of generic types (the result type inferred through the bound), static methods, trait default methods, fields of a stored adapter, and a closure forwarded to another bounded parameter; a closure that owns a value releases it exactly once.
